TEXT -256 -232 Left 3 ;#61 Resistive sampler
TEXT -256 -176 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Kk_N_TpDeo
TEXT -256 -136 Left 2 ;Rtap and Rshunt divide the through line down, and Cblock couples that midpoint to a 50 ohm sampling\nport. The through path from RF in to RF out carries almost all of the power.
TEXT 760 -16 Left 2 !.tran 0 20u 10u 0.5n
TEXT 760 40 Left 2 !.meas tran THROUGH_RMS RMS V(RF_THROUGH)
TEXT 760 80 Left 2 !.meas tran SAMPLE_RMS RMS V(SAMPLE_OUT)
TEXT 760 160 Left 2 ;Alan writes no values on this drawing, so\nRtap, Rshunt and Cblock are illustrative.\nThey set how much of the through signal\nreaches the sampling port, not whether\nthe tap works.
TEXT 760 352 Left 2 ;The .meas window is the whole saved\ninterval, 10 us to 20 us, which the .tran\ndirective already sets.
